Package: xios-desktop-stublibs
Name: Xios desktop compatibility stub libraries
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libglib2.0-0
Section: X11
Priority: optional
Description: iOS stub libraries for the GNOME desktop stack (udev/gudev/pwquality/gsound)
 Four small ABI-compatible stub libraries that stand in for Linux subsystems the GNOME
 desktop links but that have no implementation on a jailbroken iPad. They export the real
 upstream public ABI (built against the real headers) and provide small iOS-safe behavior:
 .
   libgudev-1.0    enumerates no udev devices (input comes via Wayland/Mutter)
   libudev         hwdb returns empty (gnome-bluetooth pin.c name lookup)
   libpwquality    password scoring and random generation without cracklib
   libgsound       best-effort short system sounds without libcanberra
 .
 Required at runtime by gnome-control-center (GNOME Settings) and gnome-bluetooth. Building
 the real Linux libraries is impossible/impractical on iOS (no udev/sysfs, cracklib+zlib,
 libcanberra), and the stubbed behaviour is correct for a tablet. Built for iPadOS/iOS
 rootless (palera1n/Dopamine).
